--- !u!114 &1289828498
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1289828496}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: a8b83d63ad662d944ba772861ccd31fa, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  dialoguePanel: {fileID: 887493811}
  dialogueText: {fileID: 827235926}
  dialogue:
  - You've come this far. You're living up to your reputation.
  - It is inconceivable how such a powerful man could fall into such a state.
  - I know you lost your family.
  - But this is a threat that is part of our mission.
  - The kingdom comes first.
  - That's why I didn't get involved in the years-long war between two villages.
  - You fought when the king summoned all the lords to his court.
  - Intentionally or unintentionally.
  - Both village heads will pay for this, but I know what you came for.
  - I had planted my agents in both villages before going to the royal palace.
  - We know everything.
  - And by order of the king, you will be arrested.
  - But I don't want to fight a guard like you.
  - One option for you is to take the weapons from this building and bring them to
    the head of the enemy village.
  - Maybe you think you have to.
  - But there is another option.
  - If you don't take the weapons and surrender, I and the rest of my soldiers will
    set out to end this war.
  - The king will decide what happens to you.
  - Yeah, your own village will probably find out everything by the end of this.
  - But the village will live on.
  - Otherwise, if you take the weapons away, your villagers will probably die.
  - In short...
  - Your reputation or the lives of your people?
  - Unfortunately, every choice will have a cost.
  - I'll give you some time out of respect.
  - Think and decide inside.
  wordSpeed: 0.02
  playerIsClose: 0
  interactIndicator: {fileID: 1381897331}
